# The counterfactual campaign: ~450 MB at 70k anchors in --no-thinking mode and ~2.4 GB with
# thinking, almost all of it .responses.jsonl. Regenerable in principle and ruinously
# expensive in practice, so it is a local artifact, never a commit. Added 2026-08-09 -- it
# was NOT ignored before, and `data/processed/` above does not cover it.
data/cf/
# The 52 MB the TRAINING box actually needs: the three kept-example files of `data/cf/`,
# snapshot-copied out of the campaign directory so `cf_glob` points at something small and
# shippable (§7.5.13).
#
# **THE THREE KEPT FILES ARE NOW COMMITTED (2026-08-18), REVERSING THE 2026-08-15 RULE ABOVE
# THEM.** That rule said they "move to the GPU box by rsync, not by git", by analogy with
# `data/cf/`. The analogy does not hold and the sizes are the whole reason: `data/cf/` is
# 426 MB dominated by `.responses.jsonl`, while this snapshot is 52 MB of jsonl that git
# stores zlib-compressed at **8.9 MB** -- against GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard block and a
# `.git` that was 1.6 MB. Renting a cloud GPU makes the difference concrete: `git clone`
# either produces a box that can train or it does not, and an out-of-band 52 MB rsync is one
# more thing to get wrong at 2am on a metered card.
#
# It is line-oriented text, so successive corpus snapshots DELTA rather than duplicating --
# which is why the raw `.jsonl` is committed and not a `.gz` (gzip output is incompressible
# and deltas at ~100%). Re-snapshotting after a campaign grows costs single-digit MB.
#
# THE EXCLUSION IS STILL `data/cf_train/*`, WITH FOUR NEGATIONS, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
# Every campaign writes `.raw`, `.rejected`, `.discarded` and `.responses` beside its kept
# examples under the SAME `cf70k*` prefix (§7.5.13 -- the reason `cf_glob` is a comma-separated
# list and not a glob), and those have different schemas and are ~8x the size. A stray copy
# landing in here must stay ignored. Note the exclusion cannot be `data/cf_train/` with a
# trailing slash: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the
# pattern has to name the contents.
data/cf_train/*
!data/cf_train/cf70k.jsonl
!data/cf_train/cf70k_gm.jsonl
!data/cf_train/cf70k_oai.jsonl
!data/cf_train/MANIFEST.md
wandb/
secret.txt
# PQM's Best-of-N candidate corpus, fetched by scripts/fetch_bon_data.sh (2026-08-18).
# 451 MB in four files and TWO OF THEM ARE OVER GITHUB'S 100 MB HARD BLOCK on their own
# (gsm8k-plus-metamath-mistral 186 MB, gsm8k-plus-muggle 163 MB), so this is not a size
# preference like data/cf_train/ above -- a push carrying them is rejected, full stop.
#
# It is also not our data: it is PQM's published test corpus (arXiv:2410.11287), reused
# unmodified so our BoN numbers are comparable with CRM's. Committing someone else's
# published 451 MB to get a fetch we can do in one command is the wrong trade; the fetcher
# is in git instead, and it pins the same four filenames the eval expects.
eval_data/
